From: Kristian <kristian@apache.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:10:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Read protobuf segments in chunks

The row iterator read the tag and length of every row byte by byte
from the input stream, and copied each row into its own buffer. Read
the segment into a buffer in large chunks instead and decode each row
in place; a row larger than the buffer still grows it only as its
bytes arrive, so a corrupt length cannot make the client allocate more
than the segment holds. The wire reader reads a varint without a
bounds check per byte when enough bytes remain.
